       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Andrew Woods",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Inline XML content in FOXML has a \"SIZE\" attribute. Are you ok with the resultant XML document having a different size than the source? Do you have thoughts on validation of migrated inline XML?",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "attrs": {
           "accessLevel": "",
           "id": "557058:75d3a172-f88d-4ef1-85ad-1c4a45ad0f97",
           "text": "@Scott Prater"
          },
          "type": "mention"
         },
         {
          "text": " has observed that migration-utils changes the order of some inline XML attributes. See: ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://jira.lyrasis.org/browse/FCREPO-3145"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://jira.lyrasis.org/browse/FCREPO-3145",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I am trying to get a better sense of the requirements for migrated inline XML. There is an argument that the purest migration would be a byte-for-byte copy of what is found inline. Any difference in the output from a byte-for-byte copy represents a slightly new datastream. What variance is acceptable (or even desired) from a byte-for-byte copy?",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
     "created": "2020-01-30T22:24:23.934-0400",
     "id": "21019",
     "jsdPublic": true,
