      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Andrew Woods",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "2020-01-30T22:24:23.934-0400"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:e5e5c5e0-6548-43bb-82e6-e50570cc5e41",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e5424ed15c24c95a246bac3447961e7d?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDS-1.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e5424ed15c24c95a246bac3447961e7d?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDS-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e5424ed15c24c95a246bac3447961e7d?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDS-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e5424ed15c24c95a246bac3447961e7d?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDS-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Doron Shalvi",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae5e5c5e0-6548-43bb-82e6-e50570cc5e41",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "As ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "accessLevel": "",
           "id": "557058:75d3a172-f88d-4ef1-85ad-1c4a45ad0f97",
           "text": "@Scott Prater"
          },
          "type": "mention"
         },
         {
          "text": " observes in ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3145#icft=FCREPO-3145"
          },
          "type": "inlineCard"
         },
         {
          "text": " I think the primary question is:  which should be considered the canonical version of the inline XML datastream?  The version stored on disk, or the version delivered by Fedora through its API?  From a systems perspective, I would tend to lean towards the latter, since I shouldn't have to know the internals of a system when performing an export/migration.  From a practical perspective the migration tool uses the stored FOXML, and most people migrating from F3 are probably familiar with stored FOXML, so this may not be a huge consideration.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "In our situation I am not too concerned about the resultant XML document having a different size than the source \"SIZE\" attribute, since we use in-line XML primarily for metadata that will likely be reprocessed into another format during our migration anyway.  A possible workflow for validating migrated inline XML data for a given version of a given datastream could be:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "content": [
             {
              "text": "Migrate a byte-for-byte copy.",
              "type": "text"
             }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
           }
          ],
          "type": "listItem"
         },
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "content": [
             {
              "text": "Validate the migrated copy using the \"SIZE\" attribute and using an XML validator.",
              "type": "text"
             }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
           }
          ],
          "type": "listItem"
         },
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "content": [
             {
              "text": "(Optionally) Modify the migrated copy by adding an XML declaration.  Recompute size.  Store the modified copy and new size in place of the migrated copy.",
              "type": "text"
             }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
           }
          ],
          "type": "listItem"
         }
        ],
        "type": "orderedList"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Possibly, this could be another runtime command line option.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I'm not too vested in this particular request, partially because the migrated XML is still valid without a declaration.   I defer to those who are more concerned about preservation of in-line XML, with respect to the original question of which version is canonical.  I would note, however, that to some degree this is a general question that has come up a few times (FCREPO-3198, ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3145#icft=FCREPO-3145"
          },
          "type": "inlineCard"
         },
         {
          "text": ") - should the migration tool migrate exactly what Fedora 3 has stored, or should it account for runtime transformations represented by Fedora 3 code in serving the API?",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
