       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Andrew Woods",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Inline XML content in FOXML has a \"SIZE\" attribute. Are you ok with the resultant XML document having a different size than the source? Do you have thoughts on validation of migrated inline XML?</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3A75d3a172-f88d-4ef1-85ad-1c4a45ad0f97\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"557058:75d3a172-f88d-4ef1-85ad-1c4a45ad0f97\" data-account-id=\"557058:75d3a172-f88d-4ef1-85ad-1c4a45ad0f97\" accountid=\"557058:75d3a172-f88d-4ef1-85ad-1c4a45ad0f97\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Scott Prater</a> has observed that migration-utils changes the order of some inline XML attributes. See: <a href=\"https://jira.lyrasis.org/browse/FCREPO-3145\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://jira.lyrasis.org/browse/FCREPO-3145</a></p>\n\n<p>I am trying to get a better sense of the requirements for migrated inline XML. There is an argument that the purest migration would be a byte-for-byte copy of what is found inline. Any difference in the output from a byte-for-byte copy represents a slightly new datastream. What variance is acceptable (or even desired) from a byte-for-byte copy?</p>",
     "created": "30/Jan/20 10:24 PM",
