     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:e5e5c5e0-6548-43bb-82e6-e50570cc5e41",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e5424ed15c24c95a246bac3447961e7d?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDS-1.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e5424ed15c24c95a246bac3447961e7d?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDS-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e5424ed15c24c95a246bac3447961e7d?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDS-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e5424ed15c24c95a246bac3447961e7d?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDS-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Doron Shalvi",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae5e5c5e0-6548-43bb-82e6-e50570cc5e41",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>As <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3A75d3a172-f88d-4ef1-85ad-1c4a45ad0f97\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"557058:75d3a172-f88d-4ef1-85ad-1c4a45ad0f97\" data-account-id=\"557058:75d3a172-f88d-4ef1-85ad-1c4a45ad0f97\" accountid=\"557058:75d3a172-f88d-4ef1-85ad-1c4a45ad0f97\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Scott Prater</a> observes in \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-3145\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3145\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Fix migration-utils inline XML migration to not transform XML en route\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-3145\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n I think the primary question is:  which should be considered the canonical version of the inline XML datastream?  The version stored on disk, or the version delivered by Fedora through its API?  From a systems perspective, I would tend to lean towards the latter, since I shouldn't have to know the internals of a system when performing an export/migration.  From a practical perspective the migration tool uses the stored FOXML, and most people migrating from F3 are probably familiar with stored FOXML, so this may not be a huge consideration.</p>\n\n<p>In our situation I am not too concerned about the resultant XML document having a different size than the source \"SIZE\" attribute, since we use in-line XML primarily for metadata that will likely be reprocessed into another format during our migration anyway.  A possible workflow for validating migrated inline XML data for a given version of a given datastream could be:</p>\n<ol>\n\t<li>Migrate a byte-for-byte copy.</li>\n\t<li>Validate the migrated copy using the \"SIZE\" attribute and using an XML validator.</li>\n\t<li>(Optionally) Modify the migrated copy by adding an XML declaration.  Recompute size.  Store the modified copy and new size in place of the migrated copy.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p>Possibly, this could be another runtime command line option.</p>\n\n<p>I'm not too vested in this particular request, partially because the migrated XML is still valid without a declaration.   I defer to those who are more concerned about preservation of in-line XML, with respect to the original question of which version is canonical.  I would note, however, that to some degree this is a general question that has come up a few times (\n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-3198\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3198\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Migration-utils: Configurable resolvable URLs for external datastreams\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-3198\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n, \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-3145\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3145\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Fix migration-utils inline XML migration to not transform XML en route\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-3145\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n) - should the migration tool migrate exactly what Fedora 3 has stored, or should it account for runtime transformations represented by Fedora 3 code in serving the API?</p>",
